    {
      "situation": "Making dinner · Family",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "A",
          "text": "今日のご飯、何にする？",
          "translation": "What shall we have for dinner today?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "B",
          "text": "じゃ、カレーを作ろう。あ、そこの上にある大きいお皿を出して。",
          "translation": "Then let’s make curry. Oh, take out that big plate up there."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "A",
          "text": "これ？少し大きすぎない？",
          "translation": "This one? Isn’t it a bit too big?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "B",
          "text": "大丈夫。沢山作るから。",
          "translation": "It’s fine. I’m making a lot."
        }
      ],
      "question": "What does B ask A to do?",
      "choices": [
        "Buy curry",
        "Take out a big plate",
        "Wash the plates",
        "Cook the rice"
      ],
      "answer": 1,
      "explanation": "ご飯 (ごはん) means a meal here. 作る (つくる) make; 上にある means up there / on top. 出す (だす) take out. じゃ means well then. 少し大きすぎない？ means isn’t it a bit too big? Extra word: お皿 (おさら), plate."
    },
    {
      "situation": "A free concert · Friends",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "A",
          "text": "今度の日曜日、公園でコンサートがあるよ。ただだって。",
